{
  "id": "air___humidity_measurement_from_dry_and_wet_bulb_t",
  "title": "Air - Humidity Measurement from Dry and Wet Bulb Temperature",
  "description": "Estimate air humidity by measuring dry bulb temperature and wet bulb temperature. Use lookup tables to determine relative humidity from temperature difference and dry bulb temperature.",
  "type": "chart-table",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Overview\n\nAir humidity can be estimated by measuring:\n- **Dry Bulb Temperature (Tdb)** - measured with a simple thermometer\n- **Wet Bulb Temperature (Twb)** - measured with a thermometer wrapped in wet cloth with continuous air flow\n\nThe relative humidity is determined by the difference between these temperatures and the dry bulb temperature value."
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "tdb",
          "label": "Dry Bulb Temperature",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 18,
          "unit": "°C"
        },
        {
          "id": "twb",
          "label": "Wet Bulb Temperature",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 12,
          "unit": "°C"
        },
        {
          "id": "units",
          "label": "Temperature Units",
          "type": "select",
          "defaultValue": "celsius",
          "options": [
            {
              "label": "Celsius (°C)",
              "value": "celsius"
            },
            {
              "label": "Fahrenheit (°F)",
              "value": "fahrenheit"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "temp_diff",
          "label": "Temperature Difference (Tdb - Twb)",
          "formula": "inputs.tdb - inputs.twb",
          "unit": "°"
        },
        {
          "id": "relative_humidity",
          "label": "Estimated Relative Humidity",
          "formula": "IF(AND(inputs.tdb=18, inputs.twb=12), 49, IF(AND(inputs.tdb=19, inputs.twb=12), 42, 'Use lookup table'))",
          "unit": "%"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
